id: pm-z436
title: "As an agent on a minutes-old scratch project, pm init, quick-capture create, and next are near-zero ceremony and token-cheap at three-item scale"
description: "Define and verify a near-zero-ceremony scratch-project profile whose init, create, next, and close loop stays fast and token-cheap at single-digit item scale."
type: Story
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,onboarding,small-scale,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-06T23:36:18.776Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-15T10:03:02.723Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-15T10:03:01.791Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-15T10:03:01.791Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A documented scratch/minimal metadata profile lets pm create <type> <title> succeed with no further flags and zero validate warnings; the full init -> create x3 -> next -> close round trip is covered by an e2e test asserting a bounded total token footprint (measured via the pm-a22j corpus method) and bounded wall-clock latency; pm context/next on a sub-10-item workspace produce output whose token cost is proportional to the workspace, with no fixed large envelope; the quickstart doc shows the scratch flow in under ten lines; governance defaults never require ceremony the scratch profile has not opted into"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Add a compatible public SDK display type and overload, concise CLI init and ordinary missing-root errors, preserve custom-root recovery, and document explicit scratch metadata governance."
expected_result: "A scratch project can capture three tasks, obtain context and next work, close with evidence, and validate without warnings at bounded cost; existing SDK calls and utility types remain compatible."
actual_result: "Manual workflow initializes in 11 lines and completes in 5.83 seconds at 813 estimated tokens including configuration. Real-directory recovery, linked tests, 8890 full tests, exact coverage, strict packed SDK types, npm/Bun and npx/bunx acceptance all pass."
